{"timestamp":"2026-09-27T01:07:27.468Z","ordinal":207,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0e055-1bb4-7521-bfef-3662dacd909e","turn_id":"01a0e057-062d-7071-97fd-9309f04e55db","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_08a6dfc61d4e7e62016ab86c4cf31487d0a48c72acbc16d800","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I need to correct an important assumption: a battery `.sav` is not a checkpoint at Birch’s starter menu. Pokémon cannot normally save at that exact pre-starter decision, so a Flash restore only resumes an earlier in-game save and cannot recreate the requested menu state. A restartable Birch checkpoint requires a full emulator save state (CPU/RAM/video/Flash), which PyBoy’s pinned API does not expose.\n\nI’m applying the correction discipline here because the earlier “adapter restore shim” recommendation was insufficient for the exact checkpoint you selected. I’ll inspect that rule, then revise the plan boundary accordingly rather than papering over it."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1790471244987,"completed_at_ms":1790471247467}}
