{"timestamp":"2026-09-27T01:03:59.465Z","ordinal":185,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0e055-1bb4-7521-bfef-3662dacd909e","turn_id":"01a0e057-062d-7071-97fd-9309f04e55db","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_08a6dfc61d4e7e62016ab86b7b33c887d08d70820cbfa068a9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The pinned commit changes the diagnosis again: it contains an in-memory Flash implementation and a `BackupStorage.save(path)` method, unlike active 1.0.1. But it has no corresponding public restore API. [pinned memory implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/williamckha/PyBoyAdvance/f2ff0ec6657964b9fffdbbdeeecee7043385c2a8/pyboy_advance/memory/memory.py) [backup implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/williamckha/PyBoyAdvance/f2ff0ec6657964b9fffdbbdeeecee7043385c2a8/pyboy_advance/memory/backup.py)\n\nTherefore, PyBoy can meet your restart requirement only if our adapter owns a narrow battery-save restore shim (load the saved Flash bytes into the pinned backend before boot) and proves a new process recovers the checkpoint. That is a small, testable boundary; it does not expose RAM writes to Jev. Please choose whether that extension is acceptable."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1790471035272,"completed_at_ms":1790471039464}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-27T01:03:59.469Z","ordinal":186,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_08a6dfc61d4e7e62016ab86b7b33c887d08d70820cbfa068a9","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The pinned commit changes the diagnosis again: it contains an in-memory Flash implementation and a `BackupStorage.save(path)` method, unlike active 1.0.1. But it has no corresponding public restore API. [pinned memory implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/williamckha/PyBoyAdvance/f2ff0ec6657964b9fffdbbdeeecee7043385c2a8/pyboy_advance/memory/memory.py) [backup implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/williamckha/PyBoyAdvance/f2ff0ec6657964b9fffdbbdeeecee7043385c2a8/pyboy_advance/memory/backup.py)\n\nTherefore, PyBoy can meet your restart requirement only if our adapter owns a narrow battery-save restore shim (load the saved Flash bytes into the pinned backend before boot) and proves a new process recovers the checkpoint. That is a small, testable boundary; it does not expose RAM writes to Jev. Please choose whether that extension is acceptable."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0e057-062d-7071-97fd-9309f04e55db","create_time":1790471025.727942,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21}}
