The complication is that Pokémon cannot make an ordinary in-game save at the pre-starter menu. So a normal `.sav` can restart *before* that scene, but not at it. We have three practical levels:

- No repeatable reset: fastest; run one fresh playthrough, but poor debugging/replay.
- Repeatable reset before Birch: PyBoy can reload an earlier battery save, then scripted inputs replay the prologue to the menu.
- Repeatable reset at Birch: mGBA’s full emulator snapshot restores the exact menu state.

